## (root)
#c9[i3] Requests records around 300 million downloads per week and is depended upon by more than 4,000,000 repositories on GitHub.
  > README.md::Requests #67ccc7cf87f1
#c10[i5] Requests officially supports Python version 3.10 and newer.
  > README.md::"Installing Requests and Supported Versions" #6ede94aee8e2
#c11[i3] Supported features of Requests include Keep-Alive, connection pooling, SOCKS proxies, cookie persistence sessions, and automatic decompression.
  > README.md::"Supported Features & Best–Practices" #2984d9cc92d9
#c12[i4] Cloning the Requests repository may require setting 'fetch.fsck.badTimezone=ignore' to avoid bad commit timestamp errors.
  > README.md::"Cloning the repository" #7fdec86826ad

